:\n> \n> 1. Regarding access to the larger models: unfortunately, due to commercial considerations within the company, we are currently unable to share the larger models used in our experiments. We appreciate your understanding.\n> 2. The preprocessing pipelines for SEED-V and MoBI were developed by Li-Ming Zhao within the company, and I do not have access to his original code. However, the preprocessing steps are consistent with those used for TUAB and TUEV: specifically, band-pass filtering between 0.1–75 Hz, notch filtering at 50 Hz, and downsampling to 200 Hz. The main difference lies in the slicing of the EEG signals into samples, as described in our paper. We believe it should be straightforward to implement based on the provided details.\n> 3. You're absolutely right in your observation. TUAB is a large dataset, and the abnormality detection task can be relatively simple, which makes overfitting likely. In our experiments, we selected the best epoch based on validation performance—often the first epoch—and reported results on the test set from that checkpoint.\n\nHi, I'm algo trying to replicate the resuilts from MOBI but MOBI dataset is regression task. The code of the model(run_class_finetuning.py) only contains classification task code. Should we write code for MOBI specifically?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/3299897343/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/3663791425","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/issues/60#issuecomment-3663791425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/60","id":3663791425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLF0fBs7aYQVB","user":{"login":"231qq","id":165803840,"node_id":"U_kgDOCeH3QA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u